      "message": "I think this is not good to let usb-stream_reset() or usb_written() call usb_stream_tx() directly, because usb_stream_tx() calls could be overlapped.\n\nThis is the scenario that I am concerned.\nusb_stream_reset() can be called through this call path:\n  hook_task \u003e ccd_ext_detect() \u003e usb_init() \u003e usb_init_endpoints() \u003e usb_ep_reset[]() \u003d\u003d \n  usb_stream_reset() -\u003e usb_stream_tx()\n\nIn the middle of usb_stream_tx() in this path (somewhere between line 148 and 212), if EC or AP sends some UART data, then UART interrupt handler adds data into USB tx queue, and will call usb_written(). \nSo, in this scenario, usb_stream_tx() is not atomic.",
